n  •  Slightly increases stability\n  •  Greatly increases reload speed"},{"name":"Light Mag","icon":"/common/destiny2_content/icons/736b486ddb80beefacb4f09b5ad016eb.png","desc":"Improved reload and range.\n  •  Increases reload speed\n  •  Slightly increases range"},{"name":"Accurized Rounds","icon":"/common/destiny2_content/icons/d85024478504205359c7fb52dbc4f6b6.png","desc":"This weapon can fire longer distances.\n  •  Increases range"},{"name":"Tactical Mag","icon":"/common/destiny2_content/icons/f0e309a267b25279a871d182f8910bcc.png","desc":"This weapon has multiple tactical improvements.\n  •  Slightly increases stability\n  •  Increases reload speed\n  •  Slightly increases magazine size"},{"name":"Drop Mag","icon":"/common/destiny2_content/icons/9d19f0c349652f0285bb5f999307b8a1.png","desc":"Increases reload speed but reduces magazine size."},{"name":"Steady Rounds","icon":"/common/destiny2_content/icons/6c6e1cc341487a8afd0b0c714a229255.png","desc":"This magazine is optimized for recoil control.\n  •  Greatly increases stability \n  •  Slightly decreases range\n  •  Increases airborne effectiveness"}]},{"label":"Trait","weight":3,"perks":[{"name":"Slideshot","icon":"/common/destiny2_content/icons/7d41765e3db3a77da5cce27888c52d87.png","desc":"Sliding partially reloads this weapon's magazine and temporarily boosts range and stability."},{"name":"Outlaw","icon":"/common/destiny2_content/icons/382df469a091c33e190ee583b64923e8.png","desc":"Precision kills greatly decrease reload time."},{"name":"Clown Cartridge","icon":"/common/destiny2_content/icons/794d65813703324c653878def082ca66.png","desc":"Reloading this weapon randomly overfills it from reserves."},{"name":"Killing Wind","icon":"/common/destiny2_content/icons/db2aa71ff6d808929bb0e668dcf0822e.png","desc":"Final blows grant increased mobility, weapon range, and handling for a short duration."},{"name":"Overflow","icon":"/common/destiny2_content/icons/3165fec56b59363fa974a11f5730f4ec.png","desc":"Picking up Special or Heavy ammo automatically loads this weapon beyond normal capacity."},{"name":"Ensemble","icon":"/common/destiny2_content/icons/421d6325598857bc63c1df0f25607cde.png","desc":"Improved handling and reload speed when allies are nearby."}]},{"label":"Trait","weight":3,"perks":[{"name":"Quickdraw","icon":"/common/destiny2_content/icons/6893bb2c7ec7d13cb0d91ec9dd8b6500.png","desc":"This weapon can be drawn unbelievably fast."},{"name":"Adrenaline Junkie","icon":"/common/destiny2_content/icons/6f8bde03140b53e6dc583ada1aeaa51d.png","desc":"This weapon gains increased damage and handling from final blows with grenades or this weapon."},{"name":"Firing Line","icon":"/common/destiny2_content/icons/92a5e8dbef32a414709d3196cb815d89.png","desc":"This weapon deals increased precision damage when near two or more allies."},{"name":"Frenzy","icon":"/common/destiny2_content/icons/23e06f4ced1b3e6476f342978ff5bb37.png","desc":"Being in combat for an extended time increases damage, handling, and reload for this weapon until you are out of combat."},{"name":"Snapshot Sights","icon":"/common/destiny2_content/icons/ce16c9e2cbd73bb548af3e15bdfc7177.png","desc":"Faster time to aim down sights."},{"name":"Moving Target","icon":"/common/destiny2_content/icons/40b591eae7f122fdf1cfca21fc6f6c0f.png","desc":"Increased movement speed and target acquisition when moving while aiming down sights."}]}],"notes":["Inspired by DMB PvE Podcast 25. PvE first-choice roll for end-game content. Rapid Fire Snipers are, as at S17 v4.1.5.2, the best DPS option, but aggressive frames still put out decent damage. Keep shots on target with a stability barrel, then Appended Mag gets you to the max mag size, Clown Cartridge and Firing Line are the best way to get damage out as fast as possible in a fireteam. Drops from the first (Phalanx Echo) encounter if you're looking to farm it. Recommended MW: Stability or Handling, with a damage-boosting (Major, Boss or Taken spec) mod.","Inspired by DMB PvE Podcast 25. PvE backup roll for end-game content. Rapid Fire Snipers are, as at S17 v4.1.5.2, the best DPS option, but aggressive frames still put out decent damage. Keep shots on target with a stability barrel, then Appended Mag gets you to the max mag size, Clown Cartridge and Firing Line are the best way to get damage out as fast as possible in a fireteam. Drops from the first (Phalanx Echo) encounter if you're looking to farm it. Recommended MW: Stability or Handling, with a damage-boosting (Major, Boss or Taken spec) mod.","Inspired by DMB PvE Podcast 25. PvE backup roll for end-game content. Rapid Fire Snipers are, as at S17 v4.1.5.2, the best DPS option, but aggressive frames still put out decent damage. Keep shots on target with a stability barrel, then Appended Mag gets you to the max mag size, Ensemble helps with your reloads and Firing Line gives +20% damage when you're in a fireteam. Drops from the first (Phalanx Echo) encounter if you're looking to farm it. Recommended MW: Stability or Handling, with a damage-boosting (Major, Boss or Taken spec) mod.","Inspired by DMB PvE Podcast 25. PvE backup roll for end-game content. Rapid Fire Snipers are, as at S17 v4.1.5.2, the best DPS option, but aggressive frames still put out decent damage. Keep shots on target with a stability barrel, then Appended/Extended Mag gets you to the max mag size. Overflow bypasses Extended Mag's slow reload, and Firing Line gives +20% damage when you're in a fireteam. Drops from the first (Phalanx Echo) encounter if you're looking to farm it. Recommended MW: Stability or Handling, with a damage-boosting (Major, Boss or Taken spec) mod.","Inspired by Destiny Massive Breakdowns Podcast 233. PvP first choice roll - can crit supers. Recommended MW: Handling","Inspired by Destiny Massive Breakdowns Podcast 233. PvE first choice roll - mainly for boss DPS. Recommended MW: Reload Speed or Stability with Boss Spec mod","Inspired by Destiny Massive Breakdowns Podcast 233. PvE first choice roll - mainly for boss DPS. Recommended MW: Reload Speed or Stability with Backup Mag","[YeezyGT's S15] (PvE): [MW: Handling / Stability] \"This is a super-versatile perk pool, so you're bound to find something you like. As a burst damage option, if they ever buff Firing Line, Clown/Overflow + Firing Line is going to make this incredibly strong. For PvP, as a more-farmable Frozen Orbit (72RPM), Snapshot/Killing Wind are great, and Arrowhead Brake lets you get 100 vertical recoil. On Console, I'd recommend investing in Stability if you're planning on firing multiple times, if not, Handling is quite important, as it leans more towards the sluggish Succession-level of Handling.\"","File auto generated from csv pandapaxxy-s15-roundup (tags: controller,god-pve)","File auto generated from csv pandapaxxy-s15-roundup (tags: controller,god-pvp)","File auto generated from csv pandapaxxy-s15-roundup (tags: god-pvp)","File auto generated from csv pandapaxxy-s15-roundup (tags: controller,pve)","File auto generated from csv pandapaxxy-s15-roundup (tags: controller,pvp)","File auto generated from csv pandapaxxy-s15-roundup (tags: pvp)","Chevy's S15 Super Pog PvE Loot List. Recommended MW - Reload","BRAVExHERO (PvE): B-Tier (Average). Recommended MW: Reload.","BRAVExHERO (PvP): B-Tier (Average). Recommended MW: Range."],"modes":{"all":{"rolls":[[0,13,27,31],[4,13,25,31],[4,13,27,31],[4,15,27,33],[0,13,26,33],[0,13,27,33],[0,15,26,33],[0,16,26,33],[4,11,27,31],[4,13,26,33],[4,15,26,33],[4,16,26,33],[0,13,25,31],[0,13,26,34],[0,15,26,34],[0,15,27,33],[0,16,26,34],[0,16,27,33],[2,13,25,31],[2,13,27,31],[4,11,25,31],[4,13,25,32],[4,13,26,34],[4,13,27,32],[4,13,27,33],[4,15,26,34],[4,16,26,34],[4,16,27,33],[0,11,25,31],[0,11,27,31],[0,13,23,33],[0,13,23,34],[0,13,25,32],[0,13,27,32],[0,13,27,34],[0,15,23,33],[0,15,23,34],[0,15,27,34],[0,16,23,33],[0,16,23,34],[0,16,27,34],[0,17,26,33],[0,18,26,33],[2,11,27,31],[2,13,25,32],[2,13,27,32],[4,11,25,32],[4,11,27,32],[4,13,23,33],[4,13,23,34],[4,13,27,34],